  but cannot move left or right" separates the two input paths exactly: jump is a
  press mapping driven by events, left/right are hold mappings driven by polling
  sf::Keyboard::isKeyPressed. The event path worked; the polling path did not.
- isKeyPressed reads GLOBAL OS key state, not our window's, and on macOS needs
  Input Monitoring permission. Without it it returns false forever and reports
  nothing. That is why this looked intermittent and why no log ever showed it —
  and why my two earlier investigations (bindings correct, MoveRightCommand
  moves the player 140px/s through the real physics) both came back clean: they
  tested everything EXCEPT the OS call.
- Held-key state now comes from the event stream, recorded in InputManager.
  Window-scoped by construction, no permission needed. FocusLost clears the set,
  because a release that lands while another window has focus never reaches us.
- FIVE more dead features found with the same cause: the time-rewind key, the map
  editor's camera pan (all four arrows), Pipe's downward warp and Peach's float.
  All of them silently did nothing. No isKeyPressed call remains.
- Removed the window-focus guard added an hour earlier; it was guarding a symptom
  of this root cause and the event model makes it redundant.
