  fall through the level, off screen, then respawn or game over.
- SECOND BUG found while wiring it: Player::powerDown() called loseLife() itself
  and published PlayerDied, which NOTHING in PlayingState subscribed to. An enemy
  killing Small Mario docked a life and left him standing there. Moved the
  accounting to PlayingState and added the subscription.
- Warp state loss: loadLevelByPath destroys the Player and rebuilds it, so
  anything not captured is lost. Added Player::Form + getForm/setForm and carried
  it alongside lives/coins/score.
- I WAS WRONG TWICE, and the user caught both:
  * The piranha fix I shipped last session was a no-op. emergedHeight() computed
    `mouthY - bottomY + targetSize.y` where the first two cancel when retracted,
    so it returned FULL height for the state it was supposed to hide. I had not
    checked the value, only that it compiled and the tests I wrote passed — and
    the tests did not cover the retracted state. Corrected to a single term and
    added a test that walks the whole 7s cycle.
  * The shell "damages after death" report was also real, and not what I assumed.
    PhysicsEngine applies friction to every Character; an Enemy is a Character;
    and a shelled Koopa runs no strategy, so nothing re-asserted its velocity. A
    kicked shell decelerated to a stop within a second and the player caught up
    to a "moving shell" and took damage. Shell chains could never have worked.
    Fixed by holding kick speed while ShellKicked, plus a 0.35s grace so the
    shell cannot hurt whoever launched it while it is still overlapping them.
  LESSON: both were cases where I verified the code path but never the VALUE it
  produced. Printing the actual number over the actual cycle found both in
  minutes.
