  constructed with. The constructors set a placeholder 32x32 box then called
  changeState(SmallState); applyStateSize() shifts position.y by the height
  difference to keep the feet planted, which is right for a mushroom mid-level
  and wrong for the initial form. This also made save/load LOSSY: the save wrote
  the drifted position and the load drifted it again, so a round trip moved the
  player every time. Added Player::setStartingForm() and made loadGame restore
  the position after the form. Two harnesses had been failing on exactly this
  assertion and nobody could see it because they did not build.
- WHY THE HARNESSES ROTTED: four defined their own stub Game/TileMap/SoundManager
  to link a few entity files, while their CMake targets linked the whole engine —
  35 duplicate symbols each. Two more hand-picked source lists that had drifted
  (verify_hud_boss compiled Hud.cpp without SpriteSheet.cpp). Deleted the stubs
  and routed every target through the add_verify_test helper that already
  existed, so a harness cannot drift from the engine again.
- Added NO_CTEST to the helper for harnesses that open an sf::RenderWindow and
  loop until it closes. Registering those as tests is what made `ctest` hang on
  the first one; they are inspection tools, not tests.
- ELEVEN STALE ASSERTIONS, every one describing behaviour that was deliberately
  changed and improved: death animations mean an enemy is dying rather than
  instantly inactive; isCollidable() replaced the zero-sized-AABB idiom (B-14);
  a hidden block is always collidable because hitting it is how you find it
  (B-3); a question block publishes PowerUpRequested rather than the pickup
  event nothing listened to (B-2) — that test was asserting the bug; player
  states own their sizes (24x30, 24x60); a fireball bursts before vanishing; a
  paratroopa has a one-second grace so one stomp cannot count twice.
- verify_fireball's enemy-death assertion was MISSING: it drove a resolver method
  that no longer exists and only ever checked the fireball. That is the exact
  gap that let three enemies ship with a shadowed m_isFlipped. It now drives the
  real dispatch and asserts the Goomba dies.
- LESSON: "the tests pass" meant "the two targets I build pass". A test that does
  not compile is worse than no test — it looks like coverage in the file listing.
  Build every target before claiming a suite is green.
