[2026-08-20 12:46:42] Branch: A/shadow-mario-ai-multiplayer
Git Fingerprint: 0c9c173 (before) → see commit below (after)
Fetched Remotes: yes, 12:46
Prompt: The game aborts on every clean exit with "mutex lock failed: Invalid
  argument". Confirm the cause with a stack trace, fix it so the process exits 0,
  verify with tests/scripts/shadow_chase.txt, and make the stray empty-texture-id
  warning honest.
Files Modified: include/Core/Game.hpp, src/Core/Game.cpp,
  include/Core/ResourceManager.hpp, src/Core/ResourceManager.cpp,
  src/Graphics/Animator.cpp, src/Graphics/SpriteSheet.cpp
Reachable From Main: yes — this is the exit path of main() itself, on every run.
Verified By: ran the game (three scripts + the real menu QUIT row, all exit 0)
  AND ctest 13/13. Cause confirmed from two macOS crash reports (.ips
  backtraces), and the "pre-existing" claim re-confirmed against a59d435.
Summary of Changes:
- THE HYPOTHESIS IN THE TASK WAS WRONG, and the trace says so plainly. The
  suspect was Animator's function-local `static sf::Sprite`. sf::Sprite is not a
  GlResource — it is a transform, a texture pointer and a rect — so its
  destruction cannot touch the GL context. The real chain, from the crash
  report:
      exit -> __cxa_finalize_ranges -> Game::~Game()
           -> sf::RenderWindow::~RenderWindow() -> sf::Window::~Window()
           -> sf::GlResource::~GlResource()
           -> GlContext::SharedContext dtor -> SFContext::~SFContext() THROWS
  Game is a function-local static, so its `sf::RenderWindow` member was
  destroyed during static destruction — after SFML's own statics, including the
  mutex guarding the shared GL context. Throwing during static destruction
  aborts.
- WHY THE PREVIOUS FIX WAS NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT: shutdown() already
  called ResourceManager::clear() and m_window.close(). close() tears down the OS
  window and the render context, but sf::Window's GlResource base holds its
  shared_ptr to the shared context until the OBJECT is destroyed. Only
  destruction releases it, and destruction was happening at exit().
- FIX 1: m_window is now std::optional<sf::RenderWindow>, and shutdown() calls
  reset() — destroying it while the rest of SFML is still alive. 20 call sites in
  Game.cpp updated; the member is private so nothing outside changed.
  getMouseWorldPosition() and isWindowFocused() now answer for "no window",
  which matters because headless harnesses reach the former before one exists.
- FIX 2, and this one only appeared BECAUSE of fix 1: verify_regressions started
  aborting — printing "403 / 403 checks passed  ALL PASS" and then exiting 134.
  A second crash report gave the second chain:
      exit -> __cxa_finalize_ranges -> ResourceManager::~ResourceManager()
           -> ~unordered_map<string, sf::Texture> -> sf::Texture::~Texture()
           -> sf::GlResource::~GlResource() -> ... -> SFContext dtor THROWS
  Same root cause, different owner. Game's RenderWindow had been holding the
  shared context alive past ResourceManager's destruction purely by construction
  order — an accidental keep-alive that masked this for the harnesses, which
  never call shutdown() and so never call clear(). Removing the window from the
  static removed the mask. ResourceManager::getInstance() is now a deliberately
  never-destroyed heap singleton, documented at length: destruction order between
  our statics and SFML's is not ours to choose, the real run still frees
  everything through clear() while the context is alive, and one fixed-size
  allocation reclaimed by the OS at exit is not what AGENTS.md's memory rule is
  about. It also fixes this for any future entry point whose author forgets.
- FIX 3, the warning: the stray "[ResourceManager] Texture not found: " with an
  empty id came from Animator::getSprite()'s static initialising itself with
  getTexture(""). That static was also a latent bug in its own right — it held a
  reference to a texture that clear() frees. Replaced with a per-call
  sf::Sprite built from a new, named ResourceManager::placeholderTexture()
  (reserved id, no warning, since asking for the placeholder is not a failure).
  Kept deliberately zero-sized so drawSprite() still skips it and nothing changed
  visually. SpriteSheet's getTexture("") fallback moved to the same call.
  getTexture("") now reports an empty id as the caller mistake it is, and points
  at placeholderTexture(). Zero occurrences of the old warning across all three
  gameplay scripts.
- VERIFIED: script quit, menu QUIT row, shadow_chase.txt, shadow_chase_run.txt
  and versus_cpu.txt all exit 0. ctest 13/13. No new entries in
  ~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports across a full build-and-test round, which is
  the check that would catch an abort ctest reported as a pass.
- NOT FIXED, and worth someone's attention: SoundManager holds sf::Music and
  sf::Sound in a static singleton and has the same shape of problem (an audio
  device with its own threads and mutexes). It does not currently abort and
  Game::shutdown() calls its shutdown(), so I left it alone rather than change
  something I cannot demonstrate is broken.
- Not pushed, per policy.
